    "text": "An aqueous solution of a metal bromide <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is saturated with <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>.</mo></math> What is the minimum pH at which MS will precipitate? <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msub></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> Concentration of saturated <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup></math> for <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>.</mo></math>\r<br>[Report your answer by rounding it upto nearset whole number]"
